      "metadata": {
        "change_summary": "Complete compact-lens solver. Fixes the grid-axis orientation bug found by selfcheck, uses strict upper/lower contact classification, fits contact surfaces, builds a tapered convex-hull lens with r=1.25*max(sx,sy), removes the over-aggressive positive bridging that could engulf contacts, keeps the kernel-ridge fallback, and enforces hard volume/component priors.",
        "harness_lineage": {
          "candidate_index": 0,
          "profile_id": "researcher_4",
          "session_id": "01a16cab-4e4a-71db-a3e6-89f5f0d6b42f",
          "submission_id": "researcher_4_round_1-submission-1",
          "turn_id": "researcher_4_round_1"
        },
        "parent_sha256": null,
        "rationale": "Baseline round-0 IoU 0.0698 with a domain-wide thin slab and contact loss 0.576 shows hidden truth is a compact lens, not a full layer. The candidate reconstructs a contact-consistent localized lens: the three boreholes define upper/lower surfaces and a planform hull; a tapered margin keeps volume in the inferred 2,500-5,000 range rather than the baseline's ~25,500 false-positive slab. The fallback covers non-layer/multi-body inputs. Selfcheck passed after the grid fix; a large bridging step was removed because it could place contacts deep inside the body and inflate contact loss.",
